    "turn_text": "I'm reminded of T.S. Eliot that people tend to think that some things will never happen, but in the words of T.S. Eliot, there's no such thing as a truly lost cause. There's no such thing as a truly one cause. It does give us some hope in all of that. As you've been in Congress for about five months now, I was looking at Axios analysis the other day that you are amongst the freshman class, one of the most bipartisan members of Congress. Is that something that you set out intentionally to do and to be? Did it just kind of present itself as opportunities? Because we hear so much about polarization, the inability to work across the aisle. I'm interested as someone who seems to be doing it, how it's going, and if you think there's any chance of that",
