    "turn_idx": 58,
    "turn_text": "And on those lower levels, you know who to fire, too, right? If something's not getting done, there's someone you know to hold accountable. And I juxtapose that in my mind with the bureaucracy. Well, yes. Or even just some of the way that things function within the body that you serve in the other chamber of it, I remember the senator from Colorado During the previous administration having a freak out that they would remove the memo from the Department of Justice saying that there wouldn't be federal prosecutions in states that have lifted or have legalized marijuana and demanding that that advisory guidance be replaced. You're a senator. You can introduce legislation. You can work on these things in a way that it's harder to not be held accountable if you're the road commissioner and the roads aren't getting fixed. Well, because",
